    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **266 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature. Since the acceptance test (`Cp07Tests`) creates an owner and reads `$.initials` back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the cleanest place to derive it \u2014 consistent with how the existing `displayName` field works \u2014 is in the DTO mapping, so it's computed for every owner response.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` string field to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `initials` backed by a helper method that upper-cases the first letters of the first and last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `\"John\"` + `\"Sur\u2026\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`).\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function classes were needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`RespondWithOwner` steps already run owners through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so both the create response and the GET response now include `initials`.",
